## 3. Représentation graphique

Voici l'allure de la courbe représentative de $f$ (une hyperbole) avec ses asymptotes en $x = 1$ et $y = 2$ :

```tikz
\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
    % Grille et axes
    \draw[very thin, color=gray!30] (-3, -4) grid (5, 6);
    \draw[->, thick] (-3, 0) -- (5, 0) node[right] {$x$};
    \draw[->, thick] (0, -4) -- (0, 6) node[above] {$y$};

    % Asymptotes
    \draw[dashed, blue] (1, -4) -- (1, 6) node[above, font=\small] {$x=1$};
    \draw[dashed, blue] (-3, 2) -- (5, 2) node[right, font=\small] {$y=2$};

    % Graduations
    \foreach \x in {-2,-1,1,2,3,4}
        \draw (\x, 0.1) -- (\x, -0.1) node[below, font=\small] {\x};
    \foreach \y in {-2,-1,1,3,4,5}
        \draw (0.1, \y) -- (-0.1, \y) node[left, font=\small] {\y};

    % Courbe branche gauche
    \draw[domain=-3:0.8, smooth, variable=\x, red, thick] plot ({\x}, {(2*\x - 1)/(\x - 1)});

    % Courbe branche droite
    \draw[domain=1.2:5, smooth, variable=\x, red, thick] plot ({\x}, {(2*\x - 1)/(\x - 1)});

    \node[red, right] at (2.5, 3.5) {$\mathcal{C}_f$};
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}
```
